From 3e589b261a73dc4c02e8fcc6feb2757bd8c4daf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 3dpdf <3dpdf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:33:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Measure tab: points detaching on rotation, spurious
 rotate-on-click

Two real bugs in patches/0006's Measure tab, found by hands-on testing:

1. Measured points were stored as a single cached world-space position
   (g_lastPick.hitPos at pick time). But rotating/panning in this viewer
   moves the *product*, not the camera (_scene.models()[0].setModel(...)),
   so a world-space point goes stale the instant the user rotates again --
   it stays fixed in world space while the surface it was picked on moves
   out from under it, visibly detaching the marker from the part. Fixed by
   storing (product, local-space position) instead and re-deriving the
   live world position every frame via that product's *current*
   localToWorld() (measurePointWorldPos()). Verified with two points on
   two genuinely different products (a PCB and its enclosure): the A-B
   distance stays bit-for-bit stable (68.371719 -> 68.371704, float32
   noise only) across a large further rotation and a pan, which a rigid
   transform must preserve and the old code did not.

2. Ctrl+LeftClick-to-pick shared the arcball rotate code's condition
   (mouseDown && mouseMoved), which has no minimum-drag threshold at all --
   only the *separate* pick-vs-drag classifier (dragPixels <= 3) ever
   checked for "was this basically just a click". Any incidental mouse
   jitter between button-down and button-up (normal for a physical mouse)
   fed a nonzero delta into the rotate math and nudged the model, even
   though the same click correctly registered as a pick.

   First attempt at a fix (polling SDL_GetModState() live each frame and
   suppressing rotation while Ctrl reads held) turned out incomplete: a
   human's Ctrl-up and mouse-up rarely land on the exact same frame, so a
   live poll can read Ctrl as already released for the last frame or two
   of the click and let a small rotation through right at the end -- this
   surfaced as "still jumps a little" in testing even after that fix.

   Fixed properly by latching instead of polling: mouseDownWithCtrl is set
   the instant Ctrl is seen held (at button-down, or any frame during the
   hold, in case Ctrl is pressed after the button), and stays set for the
   rest of that left-button gesture even if Ctrl is released early. The
   rotate-apply block checks the latch, not a live poll. Verified by
   deliberately releasing Ctrl one frame before mouse-up (xdotool keyup
   before mouseup) on two different files -- no rotation, and the pick
   still registers correctly.

Also: Ctrl+LeftClick now drops the pick straight into the first empty
Measure slot (A, then B, then C) instead of requiring a separate "Set
Point X from last pick" button click every time -- that button is now
specifically for *re*-assigning one slot after all three are already
set, without disturbing the other two.
